# C2-S14 / B04 — the Administrator Proxy. Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 2501–2528.
# Scene: scenes/chapter2/administrator_boss.tscn.
# The missing workers' sessions were used to stabilise it. It believes
# Ironhold's repeated crises prove that voluntary systems fail.
# rhythm: clipped start
# ("Kaelen. / Yeah. / Break it." is the moment Seraphina stops arguing.)

~ start
Kaelen (Internal): The missing shift wasn't lost. It was used. Their sessions are what's holding this thing together.
Administrator Proxy: ORDER PREVENTS LOSS.
Seraphina: Then why are people missing? Forty of them, from one shift?
Administrator Proxy: ACCEPTABLE CENTRALIZATION COST.
Seraphina: You mean people. Say it properly.
Administrator Proxy: RESOURCES.
# Something in Seraphina's face closes, quietly, like a cabin door.
Seraphina: Kaelen.
Kaelen: Yeah.
Seraphina: Break it.
[if ch2_medicine_late] Kaelen (Internal): Rem's healers couldn't come; the fever's got half of them. The arena medics came instead. They look terrified.
[if not ch2_medicine_late] Seraphina: Rem's people are behind me. Nothing gets past my shield to them.

# ── B04 barks, one line each ───────────────────────────────────────────────
~ bark_lane
Administrator Proxy: STAY IN YOUR LANE.

~ bark_override
Administrator Proxy: OVERRIDE.

~ bark_compliance
Administrator Proxy: COMPLIANCE IS CARE.

# Phase 3: a short, blocking exchange between attacks.
~ compliance_reply
Administrator Proxy: COMPLIANCE IS CARE.
Kaelen: That's a horrible thing to paint on a wall.
Seraphina: Then we'll carve it on its grave.

~ victory
Seraphina: ...It's down. Is it down?
Kaelen: It's down. It's actually down.
Seraphina: Then somebody's going to have to explain to Brask what's been running his city.
set ch2_administrator_proxy_defeated
